  "body": "What happens: The defect of #2350 (Haas) is also in five other posts. The cycle signature does not include the dwell. When the dwell changes between two holes of a G82 or G89 cycle, the post writes the modal short form and the control keeps the old P.\n\nWhere (from the review of PR #2355):\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:1071`\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:897`\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:1233`\n- `assets/posts/grblhal.cps:713`\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:1083`\n\nExpected: A changed dwell starts the cycle again with its own P, as PR #2355 does for the Haas post. A dwell that goes to 0 leaves no old P active.\n\nPriority: `P1`. The program dwells for a time that the user did not set (wrong posted G-code). It is the same defect as #2350.\n\nEvidence: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2355#issuecomment-6952300694. Found while reviewing PR #2355.\n\nDone means: For each of the five posts, tests pin two G82 holes with different dwells, a change from G82 to G89, and a dwell that goes to 0. Each test fails on the post file of today.\n",
